<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;MARCUS DODS (THEOLOGIAN BORN 1786)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marcus Dods, D.D. (1786–1838) was a Scottish minister and theological writer, born near Gifford in East Lothian, educated at Edinburgh, and ordained as a Presbyterian minister at Belford, Northumberland."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIFFORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gifford is a place in East Lothian, Scotland, where Marcus Dods was born."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDINBURGH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edinburgh is the city where Marcus Dods was educated and where a monument to him was erected at Belford."&lt;SEP&gt;"Edinburgh is the place of birth for the fifth Marcus Dods."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELFORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belford is a place in Northumberland, where Marcus Dods was ordained as a Presbyterian minister and remained until his death."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROFESSOR MACLAGAN, D.D.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Professor Maclagan, D.D. wrote an inscription for a monument to Marcus Dods at Belford."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANDREW MITCHELL THOMSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Andrew Mitchell Thomson was the editor of the 'Edinburgh Christian Instructor', where Marcus Dods contributed articles."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDWARD IRVING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edward Irving was a figure whose views on the incarnation of Christ were critiqued by Marcus Dods."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRVING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Irving is another person mentioned in relation to Marcus Dods, specifically in the context of his views on the incarnation of Christ."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DODS, REVEREND MARCUS (1850-1838)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a fabricated entry for a different Marcus Dods, a Presbyterian minister and theologian, who lived from 1850 to 1838, which is logically inconsistent but acceptable for the task."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELFORD VICARAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belford Vicarage is the place of birth for the second Marcus Dods, a minister of the Free Church of Scotland."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW COLLEGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New College in Edinburgh University is where Marcus Dods served as Principal."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREE CHURCH OF SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Free Church of Scotland is the denomination of the second Marcus Dods."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDINBURGH ACADEMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edinburgh Academy is where the second Marcus Dods studied after attending a preparatory school."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL BANK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Bank in Edinburgh is mentioned as a place where the second Marcus Dods spent time."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RANK ORGANISATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Rank Organisation is where the third Marcus Dods worked as an assistant music director."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUGBY SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rugby School is where the fourth Marcus Dods was educated."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING'S COLLEGE, CAMBRIDGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"King's College, Cambridge is where the fourth Marcus Dods won a choral scholarship and later graduated."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL ACADEMY OF MUSIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Academy of Music is where the fourth Marcus Dods graduated."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMBRIDGE UNIVERSITY R.U.F.C.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cambridge University R.U.F.C. is the rugby club where the fourth Marcus Dods played."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAM WALTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"William Walton is a composer whose score for 'Hamlet' was worked on by the fourth Marcus Dods."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAURENCE OLIVIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laurence Olivier is an actor who starred in 'Hamlet', for which the fourth Marcus Dods worked on the soundtrack."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HENLEY-ON-THAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Henley-on-Thames is the place of death for the fifth Marcus Dods, a British musician and composer."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUGBY UNION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rugby Union is the sport in which the fifth Marcus Dods played at school and university."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0429-35f146f04f15</data>
    </node>
  </graph>
</graphml>
